From: Dennis Berger <theabyssinspace@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 09:45:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] refactor(core): Make the workflow scheduler pluggable
 (no-changelog)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

`processRunExecutionData()` constructed `StackScheduler` directly. It now asks
`scheduler-registry.ts` for one, so a different `WorkflowScheduler` can be
registered process-wide with `setWorkflowSchedulerFactory()` and every
`WorkflowExecute` — including the ones the runners and the tests construct
directly — picks it up without a change at any call site.
`resetWorkflowSchedulerFactory()` restores the default. The factory is called
once per execution, after the execution is set up and before the cancelable
promise is created. While nothing is registered the scheduler is
`StackScheduler`, and nothing changes: the execution-engine suite produces the
same 1657 results.
